<title>LITHUANIA: BAT TOBACCO PLANS EXPANSION - PAPER.</title>
<headline>BAT TOBACCO PLANS EXPANSION - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-American Tobacco, the world's second largest tobacco company, is hoping to grab a bigger share of Lithuania's market this year, the daily Lieutuvos rytas reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company last year had a 1.5 percent share of the cigarette market in Lithuania. Philip Morris had the lion's share of the market with 85 percent, the paper said.</p>
<p>BAT's public relations director Ole Ernvall was quoted by the paper as saying that he thinks there are ways to compete with Philip Morris.</p>
<p>The paper quoted a local BAT representative as saying that the compnay's market share in Estonia is six percent and 11 percent in Latvia.</p>
<p>--Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
